<INDICATE ID = "T010054A069I03" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Control List</TITLE>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1">
<TGROUP COLS = "3" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_10">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "25%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "2" COLNAME = "2" COLWIDTH = "20%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "3" COLNAME = "3" COLWIDTH = "54%"/>
<THEAD>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Control Name</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Function</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</THEAD>
<TBODY>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Fuel Injection Volume Control (EFI)</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Appropriate fuel injection is performed by correcting the basic injection duration, calculated according to engine conditions, with signals from each sensor. </PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" MOREROWS = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Ignition Timing Control (ESA)</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Appropriate ignition is performed by correcting the basic ignition timing, calculated according to engine conditions, with signals from each sensor.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Knock Judgment Control (KCS)</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "3"><PTXT>The presence or absence of knocking is judged based on the signal from the knock sensor.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" MOREROWS = "2" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>ETCS-i Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>The throttle is controlled to the appropriate opening angle by correcting the throttle opening angle, calculated according to engine conditions, with signals from each sensor.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Maximum Speed Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "3"><PTXT>When the vehicle speed reaches 180km/h, the throttle valve is closed to suppress any increase in vehicle speed.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Idle Speed Control (ISC)</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "3"><PTXT>Controls the fast idle speed according to the engine coolant temperature and the idle speed after engine warm-up. Controls the idle speed by means of the fuel injection volume and throttle opening angle.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>VVT-i Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Varies the phase of the intake camshaft according to engine conditions to improve engine output, reduce exhaust emissions and improve fuel economy. </PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Electric Cooling Fan Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Controls cooling fan ON/OFF and fan speed according to coolant temperature and air conditioner status.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Air Conditioner Cut-off Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Cuts off the air conditioner compressor during acceleration, etc. to ensure driveability.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Canister Purge Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Controls the canister purge flow rate according to coolant temperature and driving conditions. </PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>A/F Sensor Heater Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Turns the A/F sensor heater ON/OFF according to coolant temperature and driving conditions.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>O<SUB>2</SUB>Sensor Heater Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>According to coolant temperature and driving conditions, the O<SUB>2</SUB>sensor heater is turned ON/OFF.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Fuel Pump Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Turns the fuel pump ON/OFF based on the starter signal and engine speed signal. </PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Cranking Hold Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Based on the start signal from the engine switch, the engine control computer continues to energize the starter via the starter relay until the engine starts.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Alternator Charging Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Controls the alternator generated voltage according to driving conditions, reducing the generation load to lower fuel consumption.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>CAN Communication</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>A communication IC capable of exchanging large amounts of information over 1 communication lines has been adopted to communicate with other control computers.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Diagnosis</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Using the diagnostic tool TaSCAN, accurate and detailed diagnosis, such as reading SAE-standard DTCs and data and performing Active Tests, is possible.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "0">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Fail-safe</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>When a malfunction occurs in a signal from any sensor, control is continued using standard values in the engine control computer, or the engine is stopped.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</TBODY>
</TGROUP></TABLE></INDICATE>
